Scenario ID: C03
Scenario title: Childcare Notices and Consent Responses
Initial workflow description:
I read messages from childcare, respond when necessary, and make sure we remember any special event or item to bring.

Domain expert answers:
{
  "answers": [
    {
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "Through which channel or platform does childcare send notices to you — for example, a dedicated parent app, email, SMS, or physical handouts — and is there a single channel or multiple?",
      "answer": "Notices arrive through a single childcare messaging app. There is no mention of email, SMS, or physical handouts as additional channels."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "What makes you decide that a particular message needs a reply rather than just being read — is there a specific keyword, a question being asked, or a request for confirmation?",
      "answer": "The key decision is whether the notice requires an explicit response. If it does, the parent submits a decision; if not, the notice is simply recorded. The exact trigger criteria (keyword, question type, etc.) are not specified beyond this distinction."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "When you note a special event or item to bring, where exactly do you record it — for instance, a phone calendar, a shared family app, or a physical list?",
      "answer": "Events and item deadlines are recorded in a shared family calendar. The partner is responsible for adding these entries. The specific platform or app used for that calendar is not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "Can you describe the main types of messages you receive from childcare and whether each type is handled differently — for example, permission slips versus health alerts versus schedule changes?",
      "answer": "The workflow refers generically to provider notices without categorising them into types such as permission slips, health alerts, or schedule changes. Each notice is assessed for whether it requires a response and whether it involves an event or item to prepare for, but distinct handling per message type is not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "When you do need to respond, is your reply typically a free-text message, a selection from fixed options provided by childcare, or does it sometimes require attaching a signed form or document?",
      "answer": "The workflow describes submitting a response and saving a receipt, but the format of that response — free-text, fixed options, or signed attachment — is not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "How do you currently track response deadlines or RSVP cut-off dates — are they stated in the message itself, and do you set any reminders to ensure you reply in time?",
      "answer": "Response deadlines are listed as an input to the workflow, implying they come from the notice itself. Deadlines and item preparation dates are added to the shared family calendar, and unassigned preparation reminders are flagged. Whether a separate RSVP reminder is set is not specified beyond this."
    }
  ]
}
